nsciousness is free and the cause of the universe, manifesting as supreme self-bliss, while in its own ground it unfolds variety by will and difference of subject and object. Contracted into mind and māyā-bound knowership, the same consciousness appears bound, yet liberation remains at hand through recognizing that I-ness.", "status": "OK", "immutable_id": "pt:pid:bodha:001", "gate": {"deterministic_gate": "PASS", "blocking": [], "checks": {"SOURCE_BINDING": [true, "candidate within 3.5x source length"], "COVERAGE": [true, "candidate covers the source"], "ABSTENTION": [true, "no abstention violation"], "TERM_CONSISTENCY": [true, "terms consistent"], "CITATION_GROUNDING": [true, "all technical terms grounded in source"]}}, "model": "beam-free", "date": "2026-10-31"}
{"id": "pt:passage:bodha:bodh-p02", "work_id": "bodhavilasa", "chunk": "bodh-p02", "verses": "11-20", "source": {"text": "pramātṛsaptakatvena ṣaṭtriṃśattattvasaṅkhyayā bhāvitaḥ sa maheśāno mokṣalakṣmīḥ pravartate tadbhūmikā darśanādyās sarvā eva na saṃśayaḥ bhūmikāḥ kṛtrimā yadvan naṭo gṛhṇāti svecchayā tadvad eva cidānandasvecchocchalitabṛṃhitaḥ ātmā gṛhṇāti vipulā darśanādyā vibhūtayaḥ cidānandasamullāsollasitātmā virājate cidvatsvaśaktisaṅkocāt saṃsāre malināyate apūrṇo smīti vividhair malaiḥ sa malinīkṛtaḥ māyīyāṇavakārmākhyair vyāpako 'pi jagadvibhuḥ vyāpī yadvan mahādevaḥ kroti pañcakṛtyatām tadvad evāyam ātmāpi kurute śaktimohitaḥ śakto vikāsāc chaktīśo gīyate tattvavādibhiḥ saṅkocanāt saṅkocitaḥ saṃsārīty abhidhīyate māyā rūpaṃ hi yat kiṃcid ālokayitum udyatā sādhyasṛṣṭiṃ vijānīyād anyā śaktiḥ sthitir matā saṃhārāt saṃhṛtā devī cidaikye 'nugraho mataḥ tadekasārāprathanāt tirodhānābhidhīyate itthaṃ sadā saṃnihitaḥ pañcavāhavidhiḥ kramāt jñātaś cintāmaṇir asāv ajñānāt kāṣṭaloṣṭavat"}, "l1_text": "## bodh-p02 (11-20)\n[and]-by-seven-knowerhood (pramātṛsaptakatvena) [and]-by-thirty-six-principles (ṣaṭtriṃśattattvasaṅkhyayā) [and]-cultivated (bhāvitaḥ) [and]-he (sa) [and]-great-lord (maheśāno) [and]-liberation-glory (mokṣalakṣmīḥ) [and]-proceeds (pravartate) [and]-its-stages (tadbhūmikā) [and]-perceptions-etc (darśanādyās) [and]-all (sarvā) [and]-indeed (eva) [and]-not (na) [and]-doubt (saṃśayaḥ) [and]-stages (bhūmikāḥ) [and]-artificial (kṛtrimā) [and]-just-as (yadvan) [and]-actor (naṭo) [and]-assumes (gṛhṇāti) [and]-by-own-will (svecchayā) [and]-likewise (tadvad) [and]-indeed (eva) [and]-expanded-by-bliss-will (cidānandasvecchocchalitabṛṃhitaḥ) [and]-self (ātmā) [and]-assumes (gṛhṇāti) [and]-vast (vipulā) [and]-perceptions-etc (darśanādyā) [and]-powers (vibhūtayaḥ) [and]-self-bliss-exultant (cidānandasamullāsollasitātmā) [and]-shines (virājate) [and]-from-contraction-of-own-power (cidvatsvaśaktisaṅkocāt) [and]-in-samsara (saṃsāre) [and]-becomes-impure (malināyat